## Schedule anchor
`ANCHOR_DATE = 2026-09-21` (a Monday), documented in [fixedPlan.js](server/plan/fixedPlan.js): `day = ((diffDays(anchor, date) mod 7) + 7) mod 7 + 1`. The old plan was Monday-first (`startOfWeek`), so Day 1 = Monday preserves that; pinning it to a constant means the split can never drift. It repeats indefinitely, lives only in code (nothing seeds the template into MongoDB), and dates before the anchor map correctly. Date keys are validated local `YYYY-MM-DD` strings everywhere; the client navigates with UTC-based `addDaysKey` so DST can't shift a calendar day.

## Set logging, references, history
- Each set is one sparse `SetLog` doc under the user, unique on `(user, date, exId, setNo)` — duplicate submissions collapse into one document (verified directly against the DB). `PlanSession` is unique per `(user, date)`, so reads never create sessions and rapid taps can't duplicate them.
- Empty weight/reps are stored as null while incomplete; typing never auto-completes; corrections after completion persist; the server validates date, day, exercise id, set number (against that exercise's prescribed count), weight 0–1000, integer reps 1–999, duration 1–7200 s, distance 0–500 km, minutes 0–1440 — so a crafted payload can only ever reference real prescribed sets.
- Progress is `done / total prescribed sets` from that date's logs (cardio never counts). Previous-session values come from the same plan day's earlier dates and are shown only as "prev 30 kg × 11" hints — never copied into current inputs. Next week's session starts empty while last week's row stays in history. The client saves on blur/check with local drafts (no remount/focus loss), a per-set latest-wins request queue, a Saving/Saved/error status chip, and keeps entries on failure for retry.

## The two alternatives
Slots live in the template — Day 1 `Plank OR Dead Bug` (3 sets), Day 3 `Pallof Press OR Back Extension` (3 sets), first option default. The display name keeps "X OR Y" visible with two chips; the choice is session-level, persisted in `PlanSession.choices`, validated server-side against exactly those ids, and both options share the prescribed set count. Plank records seconds, Dead Bug/Back Extension/Pallof record reps; bodyweight exercises never show or store a weight. Unilateral sets use one field labelled `reps/leg` / `reps/side`.

## Legacy data
Nothing was deleted or migrated in place: `Workout`, `WeeklyPlan`, `WorkoutSession` schemas are untouched. Legacy sessions still appear in History flagged "legacy" with their original snapshot, day views show a read-only note for a builder-era log on that date, `GET /gym/workouts` still lists old workouts, and export includes everything (`gymSessions` + `planSessions` + `setLogs`). Reset and delete-account clear the new collections too (tested).

